   files or loss of data through the use of this program. 

                     -- Here endeth the legal junk. --


   RATIONALLE FOR THIS PROGRAM:
   ============================
   This program was created to automate the inclusion of other phone
   directories into my current Telix phone directory. It is not an elegant
   solution, nor is it a complete solution. It doesn't sort the entries, and
   it includes empty entries as well. All it does is take two Telix phone
   directories and appends the second one to the first, updating the fields
   in the header and making sure that the entries are in Telix v3.x format.    
   The information on the Telix format is included with all releases of
   Telix before 3.20, but I am not sure about that version, not having
   tried it out yet.


   USAGE:
   ======
   The easiest way to use TLXMERGE is to just type:
      TLXMERGE <CR>

   This will present you with a prompt for a file name, which you answer
   with the name of the file you wish to have the data merged into. Then
   you will be presented with a second prompt, which you answer with the
   name of the file you want merged into the first one.

   The real syntax is:
      TLXMERGE [file1.ext] [file2.ext] <CR>

   If a single file name is supplied, it is taken as the master file and 
   you will be prompted for a second file name. If you supply both 
   filenames, the program will run with the first as the master, and the 
   second as the data to be merged.

   Basic errors are reported, and some statistics are generated as the
   program runs to let you know what it is up to.
   

   BUGS:
   =====
   None that I know of, as it merged all my files perfectly. I am sure that
   someone out there will find one, so I would appreciate hearing from you
   if you do.


